{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-76067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{6+x}+\\sqrt{5x+10}$ is continuous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our function consists of two radical functions, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\n- To find the domain of $\\sqrt{6+x}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6+x\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,x\\ge -6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the domain of $\\sqrt{5x+10}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+10\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,5x\\ge -10\\,⟹\\,x\\ge -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe domain of $f(x)$ is given by the intersection of the domain of our radical functions:\n\n$$\n[-6,\\infty )\\cap [-2,\\infty )=[-2,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nand the function is continuous on this interval." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-76067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-6,\\infty )"] ["math" "[-2,\\infty )"] ["math" "[-6,-2]"] ["math" "[-6,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[-2,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{12-4x}+\\sqrt{5x+8}$ is continuous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our function consists of two radical functions, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\n- To find the domain of $\\sqrt{12-4x}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-4x\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,4x\\le 12\\,⟹\\,x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the domain of $\\sqrt{5x+8}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+8\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,5x\\ge -8\\,⟹\\,x\\ge -\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe domain of $f(x)$ is given by the intersection of the domain of our radical functions:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,3]\\cap [-\\frac{8}{5},\\infty )=[-\\frac{8}{5},3],\n$$\n\nand the function is continuous on this interval." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-105435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-\\frac{8}{5},3)"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,-\\frac{8}{5}]"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,3]"] ["math" "[-\\frac{8}{5},3]"] ["math" "[-\\frac{8}{5},\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[-\\frac{8}{5},3]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{4+x}+\\sqrt{3x+18}$ is continuous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our function consists of two radical functions, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\n- To find the domain of $\\sqrt{4+x}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4+x\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,x\\ge -4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the domain of $\\sqrt{3x+18}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+18\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,3x\\ge -18\\,⟹\\,x\\ge -6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe domain of $f(x)$ is given by the intersection of the domain of our radical functions:\n\n$$\n[-4,\\infty )\\cap [-6,\\infty )=[-4,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nand the function is continuous on this interval." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-105436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-4,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-6,\\infty )"] ["math" "[-4,\\infty )"] ["math" "[-6,-4]"] ["math" "[-6,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[-4,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The largest interval on which the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{4-3x}-\\sqrt{x+3}$ is continuous is\n\n$\\,[$\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}$].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our function consists of two radical functions, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\n- To find the domain of $\\sqrt{4-3x}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-3x\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,3x\\le 4\\,⟹\\,x\\le \\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the domain of $\\sqrt{x+3}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+3\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,x\\ge -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe domain of $f(x)$ is given by the intersection of the domain of our radical functions:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,\\frac{4}{3}]\\cap [-3,\\infty )=[\\,-3,\\frac{4}{3}]\n$$\n\nand the function is continuous on this interval." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-340025" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340025" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340025" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340025" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{18+3x}$ is continuous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our function is a radical function, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\sqrt{18+3x}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18+3x\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,3x\\ge -18\\,⟹\\, & \\,x\\ge -6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ is $[-6,\\infty )$, and the function is continuous on this interval." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-76065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-6,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,-6)"] ["math" "[-6,\\infty )"] ["math" "[-\\infty ,-6]"] ["math" "[6,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[-6,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the largest union of intervals on which the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-x-2}{x-2}$ is continuous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This is a rational function, so it is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-x-2}{x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+1)(x-2)}{x-2} \\\\  & =x+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $x\\ne 2.$\n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded point $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,2)$ and $(2,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,2)\\cup (2,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-105470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,2)"] ["math" "(-2,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,-2)"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,2)\\cup (2,\\infty )"] ["math" "(2,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-105470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-\\infty ,2)\\cup (2,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-38831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the largest union of intervals on which the function $f(x)=\\frac{x-{x}^{2}}{7x}$ is continuous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-38831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This is a rational function, so it is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x-{x}^{2}}{7x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(1-x)}{7x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-x}{7},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $x\\ne 0.$\n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded point $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,0),$ and $(0,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-38831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-38831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-38831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,7)\\cup (7,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )"] ["math" "(0,7)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-38831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-48332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the largest union of intervals on which the function $f(x)=\\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-4x+3}$ is continuous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-48332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This is a rational function, so it is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-4x+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-1}{(x-1)(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $x\\ne 1.$\n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded points $x=1$ and $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,1),$ $(1,3),$ and $(3,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,3)\\cup (3,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-48332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-48332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-48332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (-1,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (-4,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,3)\\cup (3,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-48332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,3)\\cup (3,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-4561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the largest union of intervals on which the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2x+4}$ is continuous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-4561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This is a rational function, so it is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2x+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2(x+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded point $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,-2)$ and $(-2,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-4561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-4561" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "v