\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,1)$ and $(1,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-340050" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340050" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\infty"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340050" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340050" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340050" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-340050" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the largest interval of continuity for the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3x-12}{{x}^{2}+1}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our function is a logarithmic function, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3x-12}{{x}^{2}+1}),$ we set the expression under the logarithm to be greater than zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-12}{{x}^{2}+1}>0\\,⟹\\,3x-12>0\\,⟹\\,x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3x-12}{{x}^{2}+1})$ is $(4,\\infty ),$ and it is also continuous on this interval." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-76070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-4,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,4)"] ["math" "(4,\\infty )"] ["math" "[-4,\\infty )"] ["math" "[4,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(4,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the largest interval of continuity for the function $f(x)={log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{2x+2}{3+{2}^{x}}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our function is a logarithmic function, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\nTo find the domain of ${log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{2x+2}{3+{2}^{x}}),$ we set the expression under the logarithm to be greater than zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+2}{3+{2}^{x}}>0\\,⟹\\,2x+2>0\\,⟹\\,x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)={log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{2x+2}{3+{2}^{x}})$ is $(-1,\\infty ),$ and it is also continuous on this interval." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25cc545ce118b199073ded6344ed054eabd863cfb32a7fbe61dfc540a594989a"} {"question" "q-76071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1,\\infty )"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,-1)"] ["math" "(-\\infty ,-1]"] ["math" "(1,\\infty )"] ["math" "[-1,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-76071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-1,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979915/state.json" "file_sha256" "1076857060cce611119c9949e654b80298580fb2702983314467b1d701db7eeb"} {"question" "q-39421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the largest interval of continuity for the function $f(x)={log}_{2}⁡(7-x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/D